    {
      "id": "claim_9ef0f8c991b44797965122f373c43e98",
      "statement": "cancelTransaction runs four guards before any write: the SUBMITTED row must exist for the Transaction_ID, no CANCELLED row may already exist for that id (already-cancelled guard), the SUBMITTED row's Email must match the caller's email (authorization guard), and isWithinEditableWindow(submittedAt) must hold (window guard); only Enroll, Change Plan, and Withdraw have a revert branch — any other action is rejected as not supporting cancellation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Code/Action.gs#L544-L611",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d2362a1aeec7ffe19a6c239972e2b8bfed8d95a1050a55837adbdb03d8d60852:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b5d9423e653c44aab6d040be745c5f31",
      "statement": "cancelTransaction reverts the Enrollments fields from the SUBMITTED row's priorValues per action type: Enroll restores First_Enrolled_Date, Current_Enrolled_Date, Current_Plan, Investment_Plan; Change Plan restores Current_Plan and Last_Plan_Change_Date; Withdraw restores Withdrawal_Count, clears Last_Withdrawal_Date, and restores Current_Plan + Investment_Plan. The prior(fieldName, fallback) helper degrades gracefully when a prior value is undefined or null.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Code/Action.gs#L596-L608",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a2d7589553b214711165d0573d55fb3126c9f9deb232376bcaadc175b4361c08:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7b8195f80fee4b8a8e4cf26b0a30aeb1",
      "statement": "cancelTransaction appends a CANCELLED audit row with the SAME Transaction_ID as the SUBMITTED row it reverts, with Event_Data = { cancelledAt, originalTransactionId, restoredValues }; patchAuditEventData is then called with Event_Type 'CANCELLED' so it patches the cancellation row, not the submission row.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Code/Action.gs#L613-L653",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4e1661c8a023f2032f34899558542058af47f51c540581cbc1bb9cd1db3a1856:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8e5b890e42414a07a474cd07ea4e6060",
      "statement": "No penalty side-effects survive a cancel: a cancelled Change Plan restores Current_Plan and clears Last_Plan_Change_Date (no 6-month lock applied); a cancelled Withdraw restores Withdrawal_Count and clears Last_Withdrawal_Date (no cooldown persists, count does not advance toward lockout); a cancelled Enroll restores the four date/plan fields (the row may end up cleared for a first-ever enrollment).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Code/Action.gs#L596-L611",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0142b9d7d0efc3be9dec6f053873d1a82e3536c4bb6e6df86ed2f298b59efde9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fc4e9278381244ac87b0777a787d96d5",
      "statement": "isWithinEditableWindow(submittedAt) computes the cancel deadline as the next upcoming 15th at 23:59:59 Asia/Bangkok, constructed explicitly in Bangkok time via Utilities.parseDate(..., tz, ...) so it is correct regardless of the GAS project's default script timezone; isWithinEditableWindow is simply now < getEditableUntil(submittedAt), and cancelTransaction re-checks it before reverting.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Code/Action.gs#L560-L563",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6f8b5b793ee1f3ba61ff050f8e6076d3dcd78a6a585017dd72cee3bd2609d680:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Code/Utils.gs#L153-L183",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:05511927b7d9b2151b930dcc156b707db0e7f8cbdbcfac1d34338791797beec4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9a54c740ffe74d69919119df6af5d4aa",
      "statement": "The 15th is the same payroll cut-off boundary the effective-date helpers use: submissions on/before the 15th take effect at the end of this month; on/after the 16th, the end of next month — so the cancel window closes on the 15th that the submission's own payroll cycle keys off of.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Code/Utils.gs#L100-L121",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ee02163f02d18f74c0a3be952d51b3fa232795cbc388cbf13c87d99c2998470d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f82b7d8090684dd8bf02ecab97ab2626",
      "statement": "getPendingTransactions (Code/Profile.gs) derives the in-progress pending-transaction box purely from Audit_Log (there is no separate Pending_Transactions sheet): per Transaction_ID it keeps the row with the latest Timestamp, then includes it only if the Action is in CANCELLABLE_ACTIONS ['Enroll', 'Change Plan', 'Withdraw'], the latest Event_Type is SUBMITTED or EDITED, and isWithinEditableWindow(submittedAt) holds; beneficiary and investment-plan changes log a SUBMITTED row but are deliberately excluded.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Code/Profile.gs#L188-L255",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a9d2c98a01c98848306a6cfcf43523e7f2dc01d04a09195067d45400a1b54435:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e63971ee3f8442abb7d373d1eae32c49",
      "statement": "The pending box is the bridge between getPendingTransactions (which decides what is shown as cancellable) and cancelTransaction (which decides what is actually cancellable): both filter on CANCELLABLE_ACTIONS and both call isWithinEditableWindow, but the cancel handler's re-check is authoritative, so a window that closed between render and click is caught at cancel time.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Code/Action.gs#L560-L563",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6f8b5b793ee1f3ba61ff050f8e6076d3dcd78a6a585017dd72cee3bd2609d680:"
